.Dd May 14, 2026
.Dt PKG-BE-PLUGIN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg-be-plugin
.Nd automatically create ZFS boot environments before pkg transactions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
The plugin is loaded automatically by
.Xr pkg 8
when
.Pa /usr/local/lib/pkg/be.so
exists and plugins are enabled.
No explicit invocation is needed.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a
.Xr pkg 8
plugin that creates a ZFS boot environment immediately before each package
install, upgrade, or deinstall transaction.
If the transaction leaves the system in a broken state, the user can reboot
into the pre-transaction environment to recover.
.Pp
The plugin calls
.Xr libbe 3
directly.
It does not invoke
.Xr bectl 8
or
.Xr zfs 8
as external processes.
.Pp
Boot environment names have the form:
.Pp
.Dl Ao prefix Ac Ns - Ns Ao YYYYMMDD Ac Ns - Ns Ao HHMMSS Ac
.Pp
where
.Aq prefix
is controlled by the
.Sy BE_PLUGIN_NAME_PREFIX
configuration key and the timestamp is the local time at which the transaction
began.
For example, with the default prefix:
.Pp
.Dl pre-pkg-20260513-142301
.Pp
After creating the new boot environment, the plugin prunes older automatically
created boot environments so that at most
.Sy BE_PLUGIN_KEEP
remain.
Boot environments younger than
.Sy BE_PLUGIN_MIN_AGE
are never pruned regardless of count.
.Pp
All operations are logged to
.Xr syslog 3
under the
.Sy daemon
facility:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It LOG_NOTICE
Successful creation and each successful pruning.
.It LOG_WARNING
Creation failures in non-strict mode (transaction proceeds), and all
pruning failures (pruning is always best-effort regardless of strict mode).
.It LOG_ERR
Creation failures in strict mode (transaction aborted).
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The plugin is configured by
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/be.conf ,
a UCL file.
A missing file is not an error; compiled-in defaults are used.
.Pp
To enable plugins globally, set
.Dq Sy PLUGINS_CONF_DIR
and
.Dq Sy PLUGINS = [ be ]
in
.Xr pkg.conf 5 .
.Pp
Available configuration keys:
.Bl -tag -width BE_PLUGIN_SKIP_TRANSACTIONS
.It Sy BE_PLUGIN_ENABLED : bool (default: true)
Master switch.
Set to
.Dq false
to load the plugin but register no hooks.
.It Sy BE_PLUGIN_KEEP : int (default: 5)
Maximum number of automatically created boot environments to retain.
Must be >= 1.
Older environments beyond this limit are destroyed after each successful
creation, subject to
.Sy BE_PLUGIN_MIN_AGE .
The origin snapshot created when the boot environment was cloned is reclaimed
along with it, so pruning does not leak snapshots.
.It Sy BE_PLUGIN_NAME_PREFIX : string (default: pre-pkg)
Prefix for generated boot environment names.
Must not be empty and must not exceed 63 characters; a longer value is rejected
at load time and the plugin fails to load.
.It Sy BE_PLUGIN_MIN_AGE : duration (default: 7d)
Minimum age a boot environment must reach before it is eligible for pruning.
Accepted formats: a bare integer (seconds), or an integer followed by
.Dq d
(days),
.Dq h
(hours),
.Dq m
(minutes), or
.Dq s
(seconds).
Set to
.Dq 0
to disable the minimum-age restriction.
.It Sy BE_PLUGIN_STRICT : bool (default: false)
In strict mode, a failure to create a boot environment causes the plugin to
return
.Dv EPKG_FATAL ,
aborting the transaction before any packages are changed.
In non-strict mode (the default), creation failures are logged and the
transaction proceeds.
.It Sy BE_PLUGIN_SKIP_TRANSACTIONS : string (default: "")
Comma-separated list of transaction types to skip.
Recognised tokens:
.Dq install ,
.Dq upgrade ,
.Dq deinstall .
Example:
.Dq deinstall
creates boot environments only for installs and upgrades.
Unknown tokens produce a warning notice and are otherwise ignored.
.It Sy BE_PLUGIN_REPOSITORIES : string (default: "")
Comma-separated list of repository names that trigger BE creation.
If empty (the default), every transaction creates a BE regardless of origin.
If set, a BE is created only when at least one package in the transaction
originates from a listed repository.
Repository names must match exactly as shown in
.Cm pkg -vv
output (case-sensitive).
The special token
.Dq local
matches packages installed directly from a file via
.Cm pkg add
(which carry no repository name).
Example: to create BEs only for base system updates:
.Pp
.Dl BE_PLUGIN_REPOSITORIES = \&"FreeBSD-base\&";
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/etc/pkg/be.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/lib/pkg/be.so
The plugin shared object.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/be.conf
Plugin configuration file (UCL format).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Minimal
.Pa be.conf
to retain ten boot environments for at least 14 days:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
BE_PLUGIN_ENABLED = true;
BE_PLUGIN_KEEP = 10;
BE_PLUGIN_MIN_AGE = "14d";
.Ed
.Pp
To find the boot environment created before the last upgrade and boot into it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
grep "pkg-be-plugin: created" /var/log/messages | tail -1
bectl activate pre-pkg-20260513-142301
reboot
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr syslog 3
entry written on creation always includes the exact boot environment name,
providing a reliable audit trail for rollback.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libbe 3 ,
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr pkg.conf 5 ,
.Xr bectl 8 ,
.Xr pkg 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sasha Karcz
.Sh CAVEATS
The plugin requires the system to be running from a ZFS boot environment.
On UFS-rooted systems or inside jails without ZFS access,
.Fn libbe_init
fails.
This is detected once, when the plugin is loaded: the plugin emits a single
informational message and registers no hooks, so it stays inert and does not
affect package transactions.
This check is independent of
.Sy BE_PLUGIN_STRICT ;
strict mode never aborts transactions merely because the system lacks ZFS
boot environment support.
.Pp
The plugin opens and closes a
.Xr libbe 3
handle for both the creation step and the pruning step.
Two
.Fn libbe_init
calls are made per transaction; this is intentional to keep error handling
simple and is not a performance concern for typical workloads.
.Pp
Pruning is best-effort.
If
.Fn be_destroy
fails (for example because a boot environment is currently mounted or is the
active environment), the failure is logged and the remaining candidates are
still considered for pruning.
The transaction is never aborted due to a pruning failure regardless of the
.Sy BE_PLUGIN_STRICT
setting.
